# History service discovery

- KDB3 has a detailed history-service guide at **`_______KDB3/.cursor/history-service-guide.md`**. If the Cursor workspace root **is** `_______KDB3`, use **`.cursor/history-service-guide.md`** (see `ai-discipline.mdc` § project output root).
- For adapter layout (registry vs `apply`, replay contract, key grouping): **`_______KDB3/.cursor/rules/history-adapters.mdc`** (or **`rules/history-adapters.mdc`** when the workspace root is `_______KDB3`).
- Do NOT read the history-service guide by default.
- Read it only when the user explicitly talks about app-level history behavior, for example:
  - `history commit`
  - `undo`
  - `redo`
  - `history step`
  - `pushCommittedStep`
  - history controls / history service behavior
- Do NOT treat normal git commits as history-service work.
- If the user means `git commit`, stay in git workflow and do not read the history-service guide unless they also mention app undo/redo history.
